    "message": "Fail the intervention compiler under a stop policy instead of using rules\n\nWith SHELTERSIM_LLM_ERROR_POLICY=stop, the router raises when a call cannot\nbe used, and other features surface that failure. The intervention compiler\ncaught it and returned the offline parser's plan, so /demo-v2 still showed a\nrule result where its docs promise the error reason without a fallback.\n\nOutside an explicit offline mode, the compiler now raises\nInterventionCompilerUnavailable with the same fixed Japanese reason the\nfallback path shows. The Project intervention preview returns it as a 409\nwith code intervention_compiler_unavailable, and the legacy\n/api/v1/nl/interpret returns a 409. The fallback policy is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
